From 2de9338164ca6753ab7bef04c23f96e056a27810 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:55:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Preserve pool placement for verified hub
 continuation archives

Automatic continue pinning treats an unchecked worktree as machine-bound even when the worker published a portable workspace archive. Verify a task-scoped hub path and adjacent SHA256 outside the write transaction before suppressing only the pin operation. Retain conservative pinning for missing, mismatched, unreachable or stale references; never fall back after a failed newer archive.

Proof: baseline verified checkpoint and comment tests both fail by pinning worker-2. GREEN: 1549 pool/archive/subprocess tests, 38 continuation/archive/exhaustion tests; scripts/check all 20 checks pass. Deployment and natural continuation proof remain tracked by the implementation card.
